# Chip Measurement — Phase B: Funnel events (CORE)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (written before Phase B implementation edits)
# B1 GIVEN Firebase Analytics is linked, WHEN the analytics facade is inspected,
#    THEN `AnalyticsEvents.swift` is the only custom-event definition site and
#    contains exactly the 13 specified event names; the only custom user property
#    is `has_subscription`.
# B2 GIVEN one onboarding/assessment session, WHEN the explainer finishes, the
#    assessment first appears, and completion begins, THEN `explainer_complete`,
#    `assessment_start`, and `assessment_complete(questionCount)` each log once at
#    their guarded state transitions, never from a rendering expression.
# B3 GIVEN the persisted dose counters, WHEN a user completes their first-ever task
#    and later crosses today's frozen dose target, THEN `dose_first_complete` logs
#    only for the zero-to-one lifetime completion and `dose_day_complete(dayNumber)`
#    logs only for the incomplete-to-complete daily crossing across every task exit.
# B4 GIVEN a draft inventory and no prior packing plan, WHEN final submission and
#    plan persistence succeed, THEN `scan_complete(itemCount,cubicFeet)` and
#    `packing_plan_created` each log once; regeneration never re-logs plan creation.
# B5 GIVEN the four paywall triggers and downstream service successes, WHEN a gate
#    opens, a new StoreKit purchase completes, booking/quote submission succeeds, a
#    kit offer loads/orders, or check-in succeeds, THEN the matching paywall,
#    booking, kit, and check-in events each log once with only the specified params.
# B6 GIVEN a temporary DEBUG-only acceptance journey, WHEN the simulator runs it,
#    THEN the `[PeezyAnalytics]` dump lists every specified event exactly once; the
#    hook is removed, grep finds no PII parameter keys, the exact iPhone 17 Pro build
#    passes, and a fresh-context validator grades B1-B6. No deployment occurs and
#    project.pbxproj remains unchanged from bf3af26.
#
# NEEDS-CLARIFICATION (bounded, reversible interpretations)
# - `itemCount` uses the inventory manager's existing record count; `cubicFeet`
#   uses the same move-eligible per-item estimate and quantity calculation as move
#   scope pricing, so the analytics value matches the product's displayed scope.
# - `itemTotal` means the sum of all nine kit-unit quantities, not cents or dollars.
# - A successful historical Restore Purchases is not a new `paywall_convert`.
#   Conversion requires a verified auto-renewable transaction purchased after the
#   current paywall presentation and records only its product identifier.
# - `booking_submit.vertical` is derived from the non-PII workflow id: `movers` for
#   `book_movers`, `cleaners` for `book_cleaners`; cleaners is a quote request.
